   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Rink ice is a thick block frozen outdoors and moved inside. Each night, workers smooth it by hand with warm towels so it is ready the next day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Pipes under a concrete slab chill the floor of a rink. Workers spray thin layers of water and paint lines and logos onto an early layer of the ice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Watching the resurfacing machine is the best part of any hockey game. It is much more fun than the skating, and every rink should run it more often.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Rink ice is built in thin frozen layers over chilled concrete. Because skating roughs it up, a machine regularly shaves, washes and floods it so a smooth layer forms.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Rink ice is built in thin frozen layers over chilled concrete. Because skating roughs it up, a machine regularly shaves, washes and floods it so a smooth layer forms.$q$, $q$The choice beginning "Rink ice is built in thin frozen layers" covers both how the ice is built and how it is kept smooth, without opinions. The choice about pipes, water layers and painted logos is accurate but describes only paragraph 2 and leaves out resurfacing.$q$, 'draft', '01ac5ca6-2273-5023-9c6a-497bd7d29aff')
