   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some traffic signals run on timers, while others use sensors to detect waiting cars. Signals can be linked into green waves and give walkers a head start, all to reduce waiting and crashes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"All traffic signals now use cameras, so timers and buried loops are no longer used. The cameras also decide when walkers may cross the street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Traffic lights are annoying, and waiting at a red light is a waste of everyone's time. Engineers need to work much harder to fix the problem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Wire loops under the pavement sense the metal in cars. Cameras and radar on poles can also tell when a car is waiting on a side street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Some traffic signals run on timers, while others use sensors to detect waiting cars. Signals can be linked into green waves and give walkers a head start, all to reduce waiting and crashes.$q$, $q$The choice beginning "Some traffic signals run on timers" covers timers, sensors, linked signals, walkers and the shared goal. The choice about wire loops, cameras and radar is accurate but covers only paragraph 3, so it leaves out most of the central idea.$q$, 'draft', 'bcd50f3b-0be3-5ef5-ae54-f0623ed3625f')
